# ---- build output ----
# build-msvc/ also holds the deployed copy of web/, the Qt runtime DLLs and
# vc_redist.x64.exe — none of it belongs in the repo, and Qt6WebEngineCore.dll
# alone is 147 MB (over GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit).
#
# build-macos/ is the same story on the other platform and needs its own line,
# since the pattern above only matches the exact names: the .app bundle inside
# it is 553 MB, macdeployqt having copied every Qt framework and the whole
# Chromium helper into it, and QtWebEngineCore alone clears GitHub's limit.
build/
build-msvc/
build-macos/
dist/

# ---- logs / scratch ----
aqtinstall.log
chart-diag.log
theme-dbg.log
layout-dbg.log
*.log

# ---- CMake / IDE ----
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake
*_autogen/
.ninja_deps
.ninja_log
build.ninja
.vs/
.vscode/
*.user

# ---- local config ----
config.json

# ---- vendored TradingView Charting Library ----
# NOT published: the Charting Library is licensed, not open source, and its
# licence does not permit redistribution. This repo is public, so the library is
# excluded and each developer drops their own copy into web/vendor/charting_library/.
# (If the repo is ever made private and the licence allows it, remove this line.)
#
# The whole vendor/ tree is excluded, not just charting_library/: vendor/datafeeds/
# ships inside the same licensed Advanced Charts distribution and carries no
# open-source licence either, so publishing it here would be the same violation
# in a folder the original rule happened not to name. Nothing loads it anyway —
# the chart is fed by our own web/tx_datafeed.js.
web/vendor/
